.DS_Store

# dist/ IS committed, deliberately - this package is installed by both
# consumers as a plain git dependency (github:polotto/live-player-design-system),
# not published to a registry, and npm doesn't run a build step for git
# dependencies unless a fragile "prepare" script chain succeeds in the
# consumer's own environment. Committing the svelte-package output means
# `npm install` just works everywhere, no nested toolchain required.
# Release process: bump version in package.json, `npm run build`, commit
# src/ AND dist/ together, push.
